-- ============================================================================
-- DC25 - Rock Physics EXPERT (advanced tier) goes deep.
--
-- Flips (rockphysics, advanced) onto the DC1 deep path by inserting its ACTIVE
-- academy_course_structures row, generated from the repo manifest
-- src/content/courses/rockphysics/advanced/manifest.json (emitted by a generator,
-- not hand-typed), and seeding the six module quiz banks plus the final exam.
-- Answer keys live only here and in the table.
--
-- COMPLETES THE ROCK PHYSICS LADDER at all three tiers, the seventh app to finish
-- after petrophysics, welldata, wellcorrelation, seismolord, mapping and
-- reservoircalc.
--
-- Six modules, 28 lessons: from a rock to an interface, intercept and gradient,
-- the class flip, approximation and exact, resolution, and the AVO workflow.
--
-- Every numeric item traces to the rockphysics teaching oracle in
-- src/lib/rockphysicsTeaching.js and reproduces the live NG7 Expert capstone
-- answer key, which grades SEVEN fields rather than the usual six: brine
-- intercept 0.03434399848203321, brine gradient -0.16766246414664518, gas
-- intercept -0.06282494068620303, gas gradient -0.2565633444602355, gas class 3
-- (tolerance zero), exact Zoeppritz Rpp at 30 degrees -0.12239091302671612 and a
-- wedge tuning thickness of 16 ms at 25 Hz (tolerance zero). avoLab.test.js pins
-- the panel math to those same values.
--
-- Tier positioning: the Professional tier (DC24) owns the substitution and hands
-- over a gas case rock; this tier puts the Ekene shale (2743 / 1394 / 2450) over
-- both fluid cases and asks what a survey would record. It owns: that the
-- intercept does NOT flip because the gas sand is slower than the shale, because
-- it is not slower (it is 162.69722802961946 m/s FASTER, and the sign flip is
-- entirely a density effect, velocity half +0.028802610843132695 against density
-- half -0.09162755152933573); that the gradient is a shear story (vp
-- +0.028802610843132695, density +0.12395208861462988 and shear
-- -0.4093180439179981, so the density term pushes the gradient UP, the opposite of
-- its role in the intercept, and an uncalibrated Greenberg-Castagna shear estimate
-- takes the gradient POSITIVE at +0.084195 and the case from class III to class
-- IV); that the class boundary is a convention rather than physics, with the brine
-- intercept only 1.72 times the default 0.02 threshold and class II at 0.04, while
-- the gas call is class III at every threshold tried; that Shuey's error exceeds
-- the capstone's own tolerance at 30 degrees (0.0021746462042847164, or 2.17 times
-- the graded 0.001, which is why the exact value is the graded one) and is worse
-- on the BRINE case (0.005972095765271403 against 0.0021919285920672105) because
-- its curvature coefficient is 2.67 times larger; and that tuning belongs to the
-- wavelet, confirming DC19's f*T law on a different reflection pair (25 x 16 = 40
-- x 10 = 50 x 8 = 400 Hz ms, all sharing a peak of 0.1444934457540512, while the
-- +-0.08 pair of that course peaks at 0.1155947595834732 at the same 16 ms).
--
-- Bank standard: measured on the length RANK of the correct option and checked
-- for cyclic key sequences, answer-index skew, within-pool near-duplicates and
-- same-claim option pairs before seeding. Across the 132 questions the correct
-- option is longest in 21 pct and shortest in 24 pct.
--
-- Enrollment grandfathering: enforced_from defaults to now() on first insert; the
-- ON CONFLICT update deliberately leaves enforced_from unchanged on re-seeds.
--
-- Ladder note: an ADVANCED enrollment needs an unrevoked PROFESSIONAL
-- certification on the SAME app, so the dry-run probes back-stop a rockphysics
-- professional cert in-transaction, and probes confirm BOTH tiers below
-- (rockphysics beginner and rockphysics intermediate) are left undisturbed at 132
-- questions each.
--
-- New rp-avo-explorer panel. NO DDL. Data only.
-- ============================================================================

values ('rockphysics', 'advanced', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-from-a-rock-to-an-interface","title":"From a Rock to an Interface","lesson_keys":["l01-what-this-tier-adds","l02-the-shale-over-the-sand","l03-normal-incidence-first","l04-the-avo-panel-map"]},{"key":"m02-intercept-and-gradient","title":"Intercept and Gradient","lesson_keys":["l01-what-shuey-is","l02-the-intercept","l03-the-gradient","l04-the-gradient-is-a-shear-story","l05-reading-a-crossplot"]},{"key":"m03-the-class-flip","title":"The Class Flip","lesson_keys":["l01-the-rutherford-williams-classes","l02-brine-is-class-one","l03-gas-is-class-three","l04-the-threshold-is-a-convention","l05-the-polarity-crossover"]},{"key":"m04-approximation-and-exact","title":"Approximation and Exact","lesson_keys":["l01-zoeppritz","l02-two-term-and-three-term","l03-where-the-lines-part","l04-worse-on-the-brine-case","l05-which-one-to-report"]},{"key":"m05-resolution","title":"Resolution","lesson_keys":["l01-an-anomaly-has-a-thickness","l02-tuning-at-sixteen-milliseconds","l03-tuning-belongs-to-the-wavelet","l04-amplitude-and-thickness-together","l05-what-resolution-does-to-avo"]},{"key":"m06-the-avo-workflow","title":"The AVO Workflow","lesson_keys":["l01-the-workflow-end-to-end","l02-quality-control","l03-the-capstone-walkthrough","l04-the-top-of-the-ladder"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
